"f(a0)->'Y'","HOLD_LOT","Y","None","None","Row","C","***","@if@1","a0->'Y'","col64"
"a0.lot","LOT","Y","None","None","Row","c","Identifies a batch of wafers or units being processed in the factory.The basic format of the Lot number is: ?FYWWNNNN where F=fab code, Y=year, WW=workweek, NNNN= sequence, with the 9th or 10th characters as alphanumeric. In Fab, Etest and Sort, a quantity that has a wafer as an unit of measure and the physical form that passes through the factory. A lot starting the Fab process contains up to 25 wafers and can be split into child lots of varying sizes, and wafer losses can also occur. New lots are also created to split lots due to varying characteristics, such as speed or rework, for a portion of the lot. In some 200mm fabs production lots, the lot number uses a silicon vendor ID in the 8th character","f_lothist","a0->f0.lot","col42"
"f(a0)->'<<<dEmail>>>'","EMAIL","Y","None","None","Row","C","***","@if@1","a0->'<<<dEmail>>>'","col65"
"f(a0)->'<<<dCCB>>>'","CCB_NUMBER","Y","None","None","Row","C","***","@if@1","a0->'<<<dCCB>>>'","col66"
"f(a0)->'<<<dHNote>>>'","HOLD_NOTE","Y","None","None","Row","C","***","@if@1","a0->'<<<dHNote>>>'","col67"
"f(a0)->'<<<dHCat>>>'","HOLDCATEGORY","Y","None","None","Row","C","***","@if@1","a0->'<<<dHCat>>>'","col68"
"f(a0)->'<<<dFIFO>>>'","FIFO","Y","None","None","Row","C","***","@if@1","a0->'<<<dFIFO>>>'","col69"
"a0.date_entered__operation","deo","Y","None","None","Row","d","The date and time the lot arrived at the current operation.","f_lot","a0->f9.date_entered_operation","col50"
"a0.in_date","movein_date","Y","None","None","Row","d","The date and time the lot was moved into the operation using the MVIN transaction. Equals zero (0) if th elot was not moved in.","f_lothist","a0->f0.in_date","col44"
"a0.out_date","out_date","--","None","None","Row","d","The date the lot moved out of the operation. If the lot has not moved out, the value will be NULL. This column is used in date indices instead of Last_Action_Date as Last_Action_Date changes for every transaction for the lot at the operation.","f_lothist","a0->f0.out_date","col43"
"a0.current_movedin","movedin","Y","None","None","Row","c","Indicates if a move in transaction has been performed at the current operation. Y means a moved in transaction has been performed.","f_lot","a0->f9.movedin","col48"
"a0.current_onhold","onhold","Y","None","None","Row","c","Flag indicating if the lot is currently on hold. Y means the lot is on hold and N means the lot is not on hold.","f_lot","a0->f9.onhold","col49"
"f(a0)->REPLACE(REPLACE(REPLACE( SYSDATE , '-' , '') , ':' , '') , ' ' , '')","tstamp","Y","None","None","Row","C","***","@if@1","a0->REPLACE(REPLACE(REPLACE( SYSDATE , '-' , '') , ':' , '') , ' ' , '')","col46"
"a0.operation","oper","Y","None","None","Row","c","Identifies a manufacturing process step or a holding point","f_lothist","a0->f0.operation","col45"
"a0.movedout_txn","txnt","Y","None","None","Row","c","The transaction used to move the lot out of the operation. May want to filter where this transaction is equal to MVOU. Will equal to space if the lot is still at the operation. Sample Move out transactions include: MVOU - Move out ?was done; ?Transfer to Stores (TRST); Ship lot (SHLT); Rework lot (RWLT), 5: Non standard Move (MVNS); ?A lot was adjusted to be at another operation (ADLT);7Transfer Lot (TFLT), SPLT - Split a lot and leave the parent lot with zero quantity","f_lothist","a0->f0.movedout_txn","col51"
"a0.prodgroup3","prod","Y","None","None","Row","c","Product Classification column.","f_product","a0->p.prodgroup3","col70"
"a1.lot","lot_1","P","None","None","Row","c","Identifies a batch of wafers or units being processed in the factory.The basic format of the Lot number is: ?FYWWNNNN where F=fab code, Y=year, WW=workweek, NNNN= sequence, with the 9th or 10th characters as alphanumeric. In Fab, Etest and Sort, a quantity that has a wafer as an unit of measure and the physical form that passes through the factory. A lot starting the Fab process contains up to 25 wafers and can be split into child lots of varying sizes, and wafer losses can also occur. New lots are also created to split lots due to varying characteristics, such as speed or rework, for a portion of the lot. In some 200mm fabs production lots, the lot number uses a silicon vendor ID in the 8th character","f_lothist","a1->f0.lot","col55"
"a1.operation","operation","P","None","None","Row","c","Identifies a manufacturing process step or a holding point","f_lothist","a1->f0.operation","col61"
"a1.entity","entity","Y","None","None","Row","c","Typically identifies a piece of equipment though in some FACILITIES it might be a reticle ID. E.g., VDF027 might be the identifier for a diffusion tube at a GATE OXIDE operation.","f_entitylothist","a1->f4.entity","col56"
"a1.current_operation","current_operation","Y","None","None","Row","c","The current operation (or processing step) the lot is at","f_lot","a1->f9.operation","col57"
"f(x)->UPPER(SUBSTR( {filename} ,1, CharIndex_v2('.C', UPPER({filename}) ,1,1) -1))","lot_ca","P","None","None","Row","C","***","","SQL->UPPER(SUBSTR( {col58} ,1, CharIndex_v2('.C', UPPER({col58}) ,1,1) -1))","col59"
"a2.filename","filename","P","None","None","Row","c","","csv","SQL->a2.[filename]","col58"
"f(x)->CASE WHEN {lot_1} Is NULL THEN 0 WHEN  {lot_ca} Is NOT NULL THEN 0 WHEN  {entity} In ('<<<dToolExc>>>') THEN 0 ELSE 1 END","vflag","P","None","None","Row","N","***","f_entitylothist","All->CASE WHEN {col55} Is NULL THEN 0 WHEN  {col59} Is NOT NULL THEN 0 WHEN  {col56} In ('<<<dToolExc>>>') THEN 0 ELSE 1 END","col63"
"f(x)->CASE WHEN {lot_1} Is NULL THEN 0 WHEN  {lot_ca} Is NOT NULL THEN 0 ELSE 1 END","vflag_orig","P","None","None","Row","N","***","","All->CASE WHEN {col55} Is NULL THEN 0 WHEN  {col59} Is NOT NULL THEN 0 ELSE 1 END","col71"
