"a0.lot id","lot_ipms","Y","None","None","Row","c","","csv","SQL->a0.[lot id]","col2"
"a1.visual_id","visual_id","P","None","None","Row","c","A visual mark (laser read bar code) found on either unit (for PPV) or cartridge containing it (SYSTEST/OQA)","a_device_item","a1->di.visual_id","col3"
"a1.tray_or_carrier_id","media_id","P","None","None","Row","c","Identification of a tray within specific testing session.","a_device_testing","a1->dt.testing_session_tray_id","col15"
"a1.lot","lot_alien","Y","None","None","Row","c","Workstream lot name. In Assembly/Test flow steps it is also known as TPO, APO or FPO","a_testing_session","a1->ats.lot","col4"
"a2.lot","lot_ws","P","None","None","Row","c","Identifies a batch of wafers or units being processed in the factory.The basic format of the Lot number is: ?FYWWNNNN where F=fab code, Y=year, WW=workweek, NNNN= sequence, with the 9th or 10th characters as alphanumeric. In Fab, Etest and Sort, a quantity that has a wafer as an unit of measure and the physical form that passes through the factory. A lot starting the Fab process contains up to 25 wafers and can be split into child lots of varying sizes, and wafer losses can also occur. New lots are also created to split lots due to varying characteristics, such as speed or rework, for a portion of the lot. In some 200mm fabs production lots, the lot number uses a silicon vendor ID in the 8th character","f_lothist","a2->f0.lot","col9"
"a2.oldqty1","ins","Y","None","None","Row","n","The quantity of original units in the lot after the last transaction was executed for the lot at the operation. ?Ultimately, it will equal the number of wafers (or units) in the lot to use when computing yield. Equals Out quantity + losses. ?In MES300, on the lot move out, this column should be set to equal newqty1 + lossqty1. That is because losses could be taken at any point while the lot is at the operation. Hence no losses may occur on the move out transaction but there were losses while the lot was at the operation.","f_lothist","a2->f0.oldqty1","col10"
"a2.newqty1","outs","Y","None","None","Row","n","The number of wafers (or units) in the lot aftrer the last transaction was executed. Ultimately, it will equal the quantity of units in the lot when it is moved out of this operation.","f_lothist","a2->f0.newqty1","col11"
"f(x)->COUNT (DISTINCT  {vid} ) OVER (PARTITION BY  {lot}  )","ucnt","Y","None","None","Row","N","***","@if@1","SQL->COUNT (DISTINCT  {col1} ) OVER (PARTITION BY  {col8}  )","col12"
"f(x)->COUNT ( {vid} ) OVER (PARTITION BY {lot} )","ucnt_all","Y","None","None","Row","N","***","@if@1","SQL->COUNT ( {col1} ) OVER (PARTITION BY {col8} )","col13"
"f(x)->COUNT ( DISTINCT {visual_id} ) OVER (PARTITION BY {media_id} )","ucpm_all","P","None","None","Row","N","***","","All->COUNT ( DISTINCT {col3} ) OVER (PARTITION BY {col15} )","col16"
"f(x)->CASE WHEN {vid} Like '[empty]%' THEN 0 WHEN {ucnt} > MAX ( {ucpm_all} ) OVER (PARTITION BY {lot} ) * 112 THEN 0 WHEN {lot} is NULL THEN 1 WHEN {lot} <> {lot_alien} THEN 1 ELSE 0 END","tflag_new","P","None","None","Row","N","***","@if@1","All->CASE WHEN {col1} Like '[empty]%' THEN 0 WHEN {col12} > MAX ( {col16} ) OVER (PARTITION BY {col8} ) * 112 THEN 0 WHEN {col8} is NULL THEN 1 WHEN {col8} <> {col4} THEN 1 ELSE 0 END","col17"
