"a0.site_work_week","ww","Y","None","None","Row","n","The facility work week for the given interval in the format yyyyww.  For example: 199745.","f_calendar","a0->c0.ww","col27"
"a1.link_id","link","Y","None","None","Row","c","In Assembly/Test, the Link ID","a_testing_session","a1->ats.link_id","col25"
"a0.prodgroup3","prod","Y","None","None","Row","c","Product Classification column.","f_product","a0->p.prodgroup3","col3"
"a0.attribute_value","subs","Y","None","None","Row","x","The value of the lot attribute","f_lotattribute","a0->f12.attribute_value","col6"
"a0.lot","lot","Y","None","None","Row","c","Identifies a batch of wafers or units being processed in the factory.The basic format of the Lot number is: ?FYWWNNNN where F=fab code, Y=year, WW=workweek, NNNN= sequence, with the 9th or 10th characters as alphanumeric. In Fab, Etest and Sort, a quantity that has a wafer as an unit of measure and the physical form that passes through the factory. A lot starting the Fab process contains up to 25 wafers and can be split into child lots of varying sizes, and wafer losses can also occur. New lots are also created to split lots due to varying characteristics, such as speed or rework, for a portion of the lot. In some 200mm fabs production lots, the lot number uses a silicon vendor ID in the 8th character","f_lothist","a0->f0.lot","col1"
"a0.newqty1","qty","Y","None","None","Row","n","The number of wafers (or units) in the lot aftrer the last transaction was executed. Ultimately, it will equal the quantity of units in the lot when it is moved out of this operation.","f_lothist","a0->f0.newqty1","col7"
"a0.out_date","out_date","Y","None","None","Row","d","The date the lot moved out of the operation. If the lot has not moved out, the value will be NULL. This column is used in date indices instead of Last_Action_Date as Last_Action_Date changes for every transaction for the lot at the operation.","f_lothist","a0->f0.out_date","col2"
"a0.attribute_name","attribute_name","P","None","None","Row","c","Lot Attribute Name (e.g., GROUP)","f_lotattribute","a0->(SELECT alpha1 as attribute_name FROM @MARSSCHEMA@F_GTSData@MARSNODE@ WHERE facility IN ('IMORA','IMO','COMETS') AND table_name = 'COM$ATTR' AND key1 = 'LOT' AND src_erase_date IS NULL AND key2_numeric = f12.attribute_number AND rownum <= 1)","col5"
"a0.owner","owner","P","None","None","Row","c","Identifies the type of lot. E.g., PROD and MW","f_lothist","a0->f0.owner","col14"
"a1.lot","lot_1","P","None","None","Row","c","Workstream lot name. In Assembly/Test flow steps it is also known as TPO, APO or FPO","a_testing_session","a1->ats.lot","col24"
"a1.program_name","program_name","P","None","None","Row","c","Name of the test program run on a component tester","a_testing_session","a1->ats.program_name","col26"
"f(a0)->SYSDATE","current_time","Y","None","None","Row","D","***","@if@1","a0->SYSDATE","col28"
"f(x)->{link} ||'_'|| {prod} ||'_'|| {subs}","LOT_GROUP","Y","Asc","None","Row","C","***","@if@2","All->{col25} ||'_'|| {col3} ||'_'|| {col6}","col29"
"f(x)->SPF_FN$Date_Diff( {current_time} , {out_date} )*24","time_gap","Y:2","None","None","Row","N","***","f_lothist","All->SPF_FN$Date_Diff( {col28} , {col2} )*24","col30"
"f(x)->RANK () OVER (PARTITION BY  {lot_group}  ORDER BY  {out_date}  DESC)","SEQ","Y","None","None","Row","N","***","@if@3","All->RANK () OVER (PARTITION BY  {col29}  ORDER BY  {col2}  DESC)","col31"
"f(x)->MIN ( {time_gap} ) OVER (PARTITION BY  {lot_group}  )","MIN_TIME","P","None","None","Row","N","***","@if@3","All->MIN ( {col30} ) OVER (PARTITION BY  {col29}  )","col32"
"JOINGRID:"
